render_sheet {sheet: "C-101"}
render_sheet {sheet: "C-102"}
render_sheet {sheet: "C-103"}
save_document {path: "SR-100_labeling.rdraft"}
```

**3. Anything that failed, confused me, or that I had to work around:**

None. All commands executed successfully. The document owns no geometry directly—SR-100 linework exists only as a reference (DESIGN:SR-100), so I anchored text labels to that referenced alignment using its tangent design points (T-1, T-2, T-3). The bearing/length format matches the example given ("N 45°00'00\" E 1234.56'"). Text heights were adjusted (0.10 ft / 0.12 inches) for appropriate visibility at each sheet's viewport scale.
